// A `SignInToken` is the 64 hexadecimal digits after `?token=` in a
// sign-in link, and a `SignInCode` the six digits the email gives
// beside it. Each signs a person in, so only an `Input` or an `Object`
// may hold one: keeping it in an entity, or putting it in an `Output`, a
// failure, an event or an email, is a compile error.

/// The token of the sign-in link a guest opened.
type LinkGiven = Input {
    token: SignInToken
}
